      p2sample:"I'd like to talk about Landmark 81 in Ho Chi Minh City, which is the tallest building in Vietnam. It's located next to the Saigon River in Binh Thanh District. The building is very tall and thin, and it's made of glass and steel. Its design was inspired by bamboo, so it's divided into sections that get smaller towards the top, a bit like a bundle of bamboo stems. Inside, there's a shopping centre, apartments, a hotel and a viewing platform near the top. I find it interesting because, even though it's very modern, the design is connected to Vietnamese culture. Also, when you go up to the top, you can see the whole city, which really shows how much Vietnam has developed.",
